<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav July copper output falls vs June.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav July copper output falls vs June.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistical Office</p>
<p>reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV NON-FERROUS ORES   July 96    June 96     July 95</p>
<p> copper (thousand tonnes)	1,619	1,669	 1,784</p>
<p> lead-zinc				77	   64	    41</p>
<p> bauxite				  15	   38	    --</p>
<p>NON-FERROUS METAL PRODUCTION</p>
<p> electrolytic copper (tonnes) 11,927     12,173	 7,609</p>
<p> refined lead			3,140	3,314	 1,031</p>
<p> zinc				  2,660	1,812	    --</p>
<p> aluminium ingots		  4,122	3,658	 1,329</p>
<p> refined silver (kilos)	  5,292	7,337	 1,441</p>
<p>-- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 222 4254</p>
</text>
